  "details": "I recently started using the World Type Immobile which before now I thought didn't do anything in game as in unity it doesn't change your physics at all, it wasn't until I finally uploaded a model using it with my immobile set to .9 that I realised it did exactly what I've been looking for, making my physics no longer fly all over the place when I use locomotion. however now when trying to test my physics in unity the only way I can see how they're going to look in game is by setting Immobile to 0 then adjusting my physics after that. It would really help if setting my immobile type to world caused Immobile to no longer show in unity or atleast accurately reflect how my avatar is going to look in game",
